00:00:02.119 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start position:0%
three Eastern partners take big steps  towards closer ties with the European  Union on June 27th as EU leaders sign  association agreements with Ukraine  Georgia and Moldova the signatures come  much earlier than originally envisioned  move forward to underline the EU s  commitment and support to the Eastern  partners as President Van Rompuy noted  on his visit to Tbilisi in May choosing  the path of political association market  integration with the European Union  should not be seen as a rejection of  close relationships with other partners  it should not be seen as a zero-sum game  these Accords strengthen both political  and economic ties between Brussels and  the three capitals they include the  creation of deep and comprehensive free  trade areas opening new avenues for  trade and business they also aim to  improve cooperation on the rule of law  judicial reform respect for human rights  and other democratic values for Georgia  and Moldova the agreements will be  signed in their entirety an event  President Van Rompuy said could not be  underestimated it is a dream for  generations of people of Georgia and  Moldova and this dream comes true  now the government of Ukraine will be  completing those portions of its  agreement that remain after political  provisions were signed in March this is  the Accord that sent Ukrainians in to  Maidan square last year to stand up for  their convictions and that triggered the  crisis where so many died now their  aspirations for a more European future  are being realized
 

